    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** standing as the clear headliner. Boasting an elite score of 80.13, he benefits from a premier matchup against Dobbins, where a favorable park factor and a significant boost from his lead-off spot solidify his role as the anchor of the lineup. Joining him in the \"Strong\" tier are **Yordan Alvarez** (62.19) and **Kyle Schwarber** (61.18). While **Yordan Alvarez** faces a tougher matchup against Woo, his elite xwOBA remains the cornerstone of our offensive ceiling, while **Kyle Schwarber** leverages his lead-off advantage to mitigate the risk posed by Kremer\u2019s repertoire. **Junior Caminero** (60.55) also grades out well, with his 6% boost from hitting third helping to overcome the platoon disadvantage against the left-handed Rogers.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Dillon Dingler**, who posted a 37.83, narrowly missing our required 40.0 \"marginal\" threshold. While **Dillon Dingler** benefits from hitting in the heart of the order, his negative adjustment for dynamic platoon splits against Burke makes him a riskier play than **Colt Keith** or **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, who both occupy \"marginal\" territory but offer safer defensive floors. We are managing **Gary Sanchez** carefully today; despite his lower score of 41.99, he remains in the lineup, though his output is capped by Skubal\u2019s elite 2.77 xERA. We advise monitoring the weather, as any delays could further suppress the production of hitters facing top-tier arms like Skubal and the aforementioned rotation anchors.",
